# WhatsApp Integration Analysis — FreelanceOS × AiSensy

## 1. Project Architecture (Current State)

FreelanceOS is a **Next.js 16 + Supabase** freelance project management app with:

| Layer | Location | Details |
|-------|----------|---------|
| **Pages** | `app/(dashboard)/` | Dashboard, Projects, Timeline, Client Updates, Payments, Approvals, Settings, Profile |
| **API Routes** | `app/api/` | Auth, Projects (overview/timeline/updates/scope/closure/files), Payments, Profile |
| **Backend Services** | `src/backend/services/` | Guards, ProjectOverview, Timeline, Updates, Scope, Closure, Files, Profile, PlanService |
| **DB Layer** | `src/backend/db/` + `lib/db/` | Supabase queries for projects, clients, updates, timeline, payments, etc. |
| **Validators** | `src/backend/validators/` | Zod schemas for all input validation |
| **Frontend API** | `src/frontend/lib/` | Client-side API helpers |
| **Types** | `types/index.ts` | Full TypeScript type definitions |

### Key Tables (Supabase)
- **`projects`** — title, description, status, cost, dates, client_id, owner_id
- **`clients`** — name, business_name, email, **`whatsapp`** ✅ (already has phone field!)
- **`updates`** — project_id, type, summary, channel, sent_at, owner_id
- **`timeline_tasks`** — milestones/tasks for project timelines

### Existing Messaging Scaffolding ✅

Your app already has significant groundwork laid:

1. **Client Update Center** (`/client-updates`) — Full UI with:
   - Project list sidebar with "Active Channels"
   - Update history timeline with WhatsApp/Email channel icons
   - Communication templates (Weekly Progress, Deliverable Shared, Approval Request)
   - **"Send Update Now"** button (currently no-op)
   - **"Live Send"** per template (currently no-op)
   - **Auto-Send toggle** (UI-only, not wired)

2. **Updates API** (`/api/projects/[projectId]/updates`) — POST creates update records with `channel: 'WhatsApp' | 'Email'`

3. **Client `whatsapp` field** — Already stored per client

4. **PaymentRequest type** — Has `channel: 'whatsapp'` field

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The entire messaging UI is built but nothing actually sends messages. AiSensy integration will **wire up** all these existing buttons and flows.

---

## 2. AiSensy API — How It Works

### Core Concept
AiSensy uses **pre-approved WhatsApp Template Messages** sent via **API Campaigns**. You don't send free-form text — you trigger named campaigns with dynamic parameters.

### Send Message Endpoint

```
POST https://backend.aisensy.com/campaign/t1/api/v2
```

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "apiKey": "your-api-key",
  "campaignName": "your_campaign_name",
  "destination": "+917428526285",
  "userName": "Client Name",
  "source": "FreelanceOS",
  "media": {
    "url": "https://public-url.com/file.pdf",
    "filename": "deliverable.pdf"
  },
  "templateParams": ["param1", "param2"],
  "tags": ["freelanceos"],
  "attributes": {
    "project_name": "Website Redesign"
  }
}
```

| Field | Required | Description |
|-------|----------|-------------|
| `apiKey` | ✅ | From AiSensy Dashboard → Manage → API Key |
| `campaignName` | ✅ | Name of a **Live** API campaign (must match exactly) |
| `destination` | ✅ | Phone with country code: `+91XXXXXXXXXX` |
| `userName` | ✅ | Display name of recipient |
| `source` | ❌ | Lead source for segmentation |
| `media` | ❌ | Public URL for media-based templates |
| `templateParams` | ❌ | Array of dynamic values matching template placeholders |
| `tags` | ❌ | Tags to assign/segment contacts |
| `attributes` | ❌ | Custom contact attributes |

**Response:** `200` on success.

### Webhook Topics (Real-time events)

Set up webhook subscriptions in AiSensy to receive:

| Topic | Trigger |
|-------|---------|
| `message.created` | New message sent by assistant, agent, user, or broadcast |
| `message.status.updated` | Message status changes (sent → delivered → read) |
| `message.sender.user` | **User replies** to your business on WhatsApp |
| `contact.created` | New contact added |
| `contact.attribute.revised` | Contact attributes updated |

---

## 3. What to Set Up in Your AiSensy Account

### Step 1: Get Your API Key
1. Log in to [AiSensy Dashboard](https://app.aisensy.com)
2. Go to **Manage → API Key**
3. Copy the API key
4. Add to your `.env.local`:
   ```
   AISENSY_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
   ```

### Step 2: Create WhatsApp Message Templates

You need **pre-approved templates** for each type of message. Create these in AiSensy:

| Template Name | Use Case | Suggested Body | Parameters |
|--------------|----------|----------------|------------|
| `project_weekly_update` | Weekly progress | `Hi {{1}}! Here's your weekly update for {{2}}: {{3}}` | clientName, projectTitle, summary |
| `deliverable_shared` | Sharing deliverables | `Hi {{1}}! A new deliverable for {{2}} is ready: {{3}}` | clientName, projectTitle, details |
| `approval_request` | Requesting approval | `Hi {{1}}, we need your approval on {{2}} for {{3}}. Please review.` | clientName, milestone, projectTitle |
| `payment_reminder` | Payment due | `Hi {{1}}, a payment of {{2}} {{3}} for {{4}} is due on {{5}}.` | clientName, amount, currency, projectTitle, dueDate |
| `project_milestone_complete` | Milestone done | `Great news {{1}}! Milestone "{{2}}" for {{3}} is now complete.` | clientName, milestoneName, projectTitle |
| `buffer_update` | Buffer/delay notification | `Hi {{1}}, an update on {{2}}: {{3}}` | clientName, projectTitle, details |

> [!WARNING]
> WhatsApp templates must be **submitted for approval** and can take 24-48 hours. Start this process first since the templates need to be approved before you can create API campaigns.

### Step 3: Create API Campaigns

For **each approved template**, create an API Campaign:

1. Go to **Campaigns** in AiSensy
2. Click **Create Campaign** → Select **API Campaign**
3. **Campaign Name** — use a clear name matching the template (e.g., `project_weekly_update`)
4. **Select Template** — pick the approved template
5. **Set campaign status to "Live"**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `campaignName` in your API call must **exactly match** the campaign name you create here.

### Step 4: Set Up Webhooks (for delivery tracking & client replies)

1. In AiSensy Dashboard, go to **Settings → Webhooks**
2. **Webhook URL**: Use ngrok for development:
   ```bash
   ngrok http 3000
   ```
   Your webhook URL will be: `https://your-ngrok-subdomain.ngrok-free.app/api/webhooks/aisensy`
3. **Subscribe to topics:**
   - ✅ `message.status.updated` — Track delivery (sent → delivered → read)
   - ✅ `message.sender.user` — Receive client replies
   - ✅ `message.created` — Track all messages

### Step 5: Create Contact Attributes (Optional but Recommended)

In AiSensy Dashboard → **Manage → Attributes**, add:
- `project_name` (string)
- `freelancer_name` (string)
- `project_status` (string)

These help segment contacts within AiSensy.

---

## 4. What to Build in FreelanceOS

### Phase 1 — Core Messaging (Wire up existing UI)

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **New env vars** | `AISENSY_API_KEY` in `.env.local` |
| **New service** | `src/backend/services/whatsappService.ts` — wraps AiSensy API calls |
| **New API route** | `app/api/whatsapp/send/route.ts` — endpoint to trigger messages |
| **New API route** | `app/api/webhooks/aisensy/route.ts` — receive webhooks (no JWT) |
| **DB migration** | Add `whatsapp_status` column to `updates` table (sent/delivered/read/failed) |
| **Wire Update Panel** | Connect "Send Update Now" and "Live Send" buttons → call `/api/whatsapp/send` |
| **Wire update history** | Show delivery status badges based on `whatsapp_status` |

### Phase 2 — Delivery Tracking & Replies

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Webhook handler** | Process `message.status.updated` → update `whatsapp_status` in DB |
| **Client replies** | Process `message.sender.user` → store as incoming messages |
| **New DB table** | `whatsapp_messages` — full message log with status tracking |
| **Real-time UI** | Show delivery receipts (✓ sent, ✓✓ delivered, blue ✓✓ read) |

### Phase 3 — Auto-Send & Payment Reminders

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Auto-send logic** | Cron/scheduled function for weekly auto-updates |
| **Payment reminders** | Wire payment due notifications to WhatsApp |
| **Approval requests** | Send milestone approval requests via WhatsApp |

---

## 5. Environment Variables Summary

Add these to `.env.local`:

```env
# AiSensy WhatsApp Integration
AISENSY_API_KEY=your_aisensy_api_key
AISENSY_API_URL=https://backend.aisensy.com/campaign/t1/api/v2

# Webhook (for development with ngrok)  
WEBHOOK_SECRET=a_random_secret_for_verification
```

---

## 6. Prerequisites Checklist

- [ ] **AiSensy account** with WhatsApp Business API verified
- [ ] **API Key** copied from AiSensy Dashboard → Manage → API Key
- [ ] **6 WhatsApp templates** created and submitted for approval (see table in Step 2)
- [ ] **6 API Campaigns** created (one per template), all set to **Live**
- [ ] **Webhook subscription** configured with ngrok URL
- [ ] **ngrok** installed and running: `ngrok http 3000`
- [ ] **Env vars** added to `.env.local`
- [ ] **Contact attributes** created in AiSensy (optional)

---

## 7. Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant FE as FreelanceOS UI
    participant API as Next.js API Routes
    participant WS as WhatsApp Service
    participant AS as AiSensy API
    participant WA as WhatsApp
    participant CL as Client Phone

    FE->>API: POST /api/whatsapp/send
    API->>WS: sendTemplateMessage()
    WS->>AS: POST /campaign/t1/api/v2
    AS->>WA: Send Template Message
    WA->>CL: WhatsApp Message Delivered
    
    Note over AS,API: Webhook: message.status.updated
    AS-->>API: POST /api/webhooks/aisensy
    API->>WS: updateMessageStatus()
    
    Note over CL,AS: Client replies
    CL->>WA: Reply Message
    WA->>AS: Incoming Message
    AS-->>API: POST /api/webhooks/aisensy
    API->>WS: storeIncomingMessage()
```

---

## 8. Key Constraints & Notes

> [!CAUTION]
> - WhatsApp **only allows template messages** for business-initiated conversations. Free-form text is only possible within a 24-hour reply window.
> - Template parameters array length must **exactly match** the number of placeholders in the template, or the API will reject the request.
> - Media URLs in templates must be **publicly accessible**.
> - The AiSensy API key should **never** be exposed client-side — all calls must go through your Next.js API routes.

> [!NOTE]
> - If a destination number doesn't exist in AiSensy contacts, a new contact is **automatically created**.
> - For Indian numbers, `+91` prefix is optional. For all other countries, country code is mandatory.
> - Tags and attributes must be pre-created in AiSensy before they can be used in API calls.
